# Automation Suite Project Rules

Before any project work, read `AI-USAGE.md` in full. It is the authoritative project protocol; this rule only adapts it for Cursor.

At session start, inspect `cases/<slug>/state.json` and continue from `next_steps`. When no case applies, use or create `cases/ad-hoc/`. State the concrete artifact to obtain before implementation.

Consult `kb/**/techniques/` and the matching project skill before implementing. Use `rg --files` and local validation scripts for inventory, and perform static decrypt/deobfuscate checks before handling protected code.

Use PowerShell with literal paths. Preserve existing changes, check Git status before writing, and never overwrite source artifacts. Do not execute unknown payloads. Keep secrets in `.env`, access them through environment variables, and keep `.env` ignored by Git.

Do not delete files, commit, push, publish, or share content without explicit authorization. Keep changes within the request. Store relevant artifacts in `exports/` or `reports/`, preserve originals with backups, and include paths plus hashes, signals, or verification commands in every conclusion.
